SOFT family files cached from GEO FTP for GeoSingleCellDetectorTest etc.
Raw downloads come from ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/{GSE*nnn}/{GSE*}/soft/{GSE*}_family.soft.gz

The following fixtures have been chopped to reduce FTP probe fanout
during GeoSingleCellDetectorTest slow runs (per-supplementary-archive
FTP open + entry enumeration dominates wall-clock; see
handoffs/SLOW_SURVIVORS_PERF_PROBE_2026_05_23.md).

GSE109774_family.soft.gz — kept only the FIRST !Series_supplementary_file
TAR (Bladder); dropped 18 other organ-level TARs. Samples (46) kept verbatim
since their !Sample_supplementary_file = NONE so they contribute zero
network probes. Detector still finds single-cell data via the one TAR
that remains.

GSE196516_family.soft.gz — kept 2 of 12 ^SAMPLE blocks (GSM5885669, an
ATAC-seq sample, + GSM5885676, the first scRNA-Seq sample). !Series_sample_id
list pruned to match. Test only asserts hasSingleCellData == true and
getSingleCellDataType == MEX; one transcriptomic sample is enough to
satisfy the MEX detector.

GSE201032_family.soft.gz — kept 1 of 8 ^SAMPLE blocks (GSM6049315).
!Series_sample_id list pruned. Test assertion in testGSE201032()
updated from hasSize(8) to hasSize(1) accordingly. All 8 original
samples shared the same series-level metadata supplementary, so a
single sample exercises the same code path.

Regen recipe (one-shot Python, NOT in repo):

  import gzip, sys
  def chop_by_samples(lines, keep_accessions):
      out, in_sample, keep_current = [], False, False
      for line in lines:
          if line.startswith("^SAMPLE"):
              in_sample = True
              acc = line.split("=",1)[1].strip()
              keep_current = acc in keep_accessions
              if keep_current: out.append(line)
              continue
          if in_sample:
              if line.startswith("^"):
                  in_sample = False
              else:
                  if keep_current: out.append(line)
                  continue
          if line.startswith("!Series_sample_id"):
              if line.split("=",1)[1].strip() in keep_accessions:
                  out.append(line)
          else:
              out.append(line)
      return out

To refresh from upstream, re-download from
ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/{GSE*nnn}/{GSE*}/soft/{GSE*}_family.soft.gz
and re-apply the chop.
